WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.220
Hackers sent false nuclear and chemical warnings to civilians in Ukraine and Russia Sunday. This is Omni View, episode 224. Hebron after an army pullback, food cuts in Sudan's camps, Taiwan's complaint about a meeting invitation, then understanding the issue. Ukraine's air alert app warned of nuclear radiation danger in Kiev and of potential street combat. France 24 reports that Russia's emergency ministry app also sent false alerts after unauthorized access.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.620
and that both countries' tools were reached with specific false messages, civilians who

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.100
keep that Ukrainian mobile emergency tool on their phones received the key warnings as

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.760
official notices. Ukrainian authorities clarified there was no radiation threat, and they issued

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.080
that all clear within an hour of the messages appearing. Ukraine's Air Force stated on telegram

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.520
that the app had been subjected to enemy influence. Ukraine's Center for Strategic Communications

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.540
politicians pointed to Russian language phrasing in one message as evidence of the source.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.840
Russian officials described the event as a hack that sent fake emergency alerts, and

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.160
they did not name an attacker.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.280
Core communication channels that civilians use every day in a war zone were the target,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.520
the Guardian writes, with disinformation placed among broader efforts to affect civilian

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.160
resilience.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.200
Kiev's public case for a culprit is that wording plus a charge of enemy influence.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.460
Once Moscow's public case is that its own ministry app was breached, and it stops there,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.780
with no name attached.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.920
A brief local ceasefire in occupied Karsan ended the same day.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.840
Those six days had allowed limited humanitarian access, including some evacuations and aid.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.800
When that pause closed, those narrow corridors closed with it.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.570
Israeli forces withdrew from a neighborhood in occupied Hebron on Monday.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:52.450
The West Bank operation had begun after the killing of two soldiers in late October.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.830
More than 3,000 residents had been displaced during the raid, and many began returning

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:03.630
to damaged homes. Soldiers conducted searches, detained suspects, and confiscated four weapons

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:09.050
along with vests and additional military equipment. They demolished the attacker's homes before

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:14.210
pulling back. A military official stated that counterterrorism activities continue across

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:20.010
the West Bank. That official said the withdrawal occurred after all operational activities had concluded.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.330
Residents described returning to ransacked apartments with furniture,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:28.850
strewn, and personal items damaged, including a child's bicycle that was broken.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.230
That emptied neighborhood was where the two gunmen had lived.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:36.650
Those gunmen had attacked an army checkpoint near Hebron on October 23.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:41.670
Hebron's municipality said the displacement came during the clearance of the assailants

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:46.790
neighborhood. Families walking back in said they met damaged rooms and ordinary objects

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:51.890
already broken. Detentions and weapon seizures were listed by the army among the results

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.629
before the troops left. Aisha Adam, a 50-year-old woman who fled

00:02:56.629 --> 00:03:02.549
Cartoum, says assistance has fallen at her current site in Port Sudan. Al-Jazeera reports

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:07.969
that she now needs paid work to feed two children in her care, as displaced Sudanese and camps

00:03:07.969 --> 00:03:13.769
face sharp cuts and warnings of famine grow. Sudan's war between the Sudanese armed forces and

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:19.949
the rapid support forces has driven 13 million people from their homes and left as many as 200,000

00:03:19.949 --> 00:03:26.129
dead. A joint United States State Department statement on October 27th warned of deteriorating

00:03:26.129 --> 00:03:31.789
food security and the risk of famine in coming months. Aid at newer displacement sites has decreased

00:03:31.789 --> 00:03:37.389
trees compared with earlier shelters, forcing residents to seek paid work. Aisha Adam first

00:03:37.389 --> 00:03:41.849
stayed at a central shelter in Port Sudan, then was moved to an outskirts site where

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:47.229
help dropped sharply. That United States statement called the slide in food availability alarming

00:03:47.229 --> 00:03:52.589
and asked for urgent action, fighting followed her from Cartoum to Omderman and then to the

00:03:52.589 --> 00:03:58.069
Port Sudan camp. She lives there with her orphaned grandson and nephew, the two children now

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:04.208
depending on thinner rations and whatever work she can find. Taiwan said China breached protocol by

00:04:04.208 --> 00:04:10.188
sending an emailed invitation to an upcoming Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation, or APEC meeting.

00:04:10.988 --> 00:04:15.508
Bloomberg reports that Taipei sees the method as diminishing the island's status and sliding

00:04:15.508 --> 00:04:20.468
President Leichingte, and as an attempt to lower Taiwan's standing ahead of the gathering.

00:04:21.088 --> 00:04:25.048
Taiwan maintains it should receive the same formal treatment as other participants.

00:04:25.048 --> 00:04:30.288
Taipei criticized the emailed format as a departure from standard diplomatic practice

00:04:30.288 --> 00:04:31.508
for APEC invitations.

00:04:32.148 --> 00:04:37.168
This complaint sits against Beijing's long-standing position that Taiwan is part of China.

00:04:37.788 --> 00:04:42.388
Everything turns on whether an emailed invite is ordinary logistics or a deliberate cut

00:04:42.388 --> 00:04:42.848
in rank.

00:04:43.528 --> 00:04:47.928
Beijing, in Taipei's reading, slided both the President and the island's standing through

00:04:47.928 --> 00:04:49.288
the choice of delivery method.

00:04:49.928 --> 00:04:54.768
How Taiwan is invited into international forums is itself a running argument, because

00:04:54.768 --> 00:05:00.208
China seeks to limit the island's visibility. The slight, as Taipei describes it, is in

00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:04.948
the delivery method itself rather than in weather and invitation arrived. An upcoming

00:05:04.948 --> 00:05:10.882
APEC meeting is the venue, and the argument is about status on the way in. Indian government

00:05:10.882 --> 00:05:16.442
bonds rallied on Monday as crude oil prices extended losses. It was their strongest stretch

00:05:16.442 --> 00:05:22.702
of gains in six months. Falling crude eased inflation concerns for India, a fuel importing country

00:05:22.702 --> 00:05:27.962
that buys most of its oil abroad. Lower oil prices reduce pressure on India's import

00:05:27.962 --> 00:05:33.442
bill. They also lighten the inflation outlook that bond investors watch. Higher yields on

00:05:33.442 --> 00:05:38.562
the bonds drew additional buyer interest. An economy that relies on imported energy tends

00:05:38.562 --> 00:05:44.762
to see its local bonds move when global crude moves. Inflation worries tied to fuel receded as oil

00:05:44.762 --> 00:05:51.992
kept falling, and buyers treated that as room to step in. Workers at IDBI bank limited argue that a

00:05:51.992 --> 00:05:57.212
sale to Fairfax financial holdings limited, threatens job security and public control of

00:05:57.212 --> 00:06:02.052
a major bank. They launched a nationwide strike on Monday and called on the federal government

00:06:02.052 --> 00:06:07.372
to cancel the privatization. The two-day action is a direct response to the proposed transfer

00:06:07.372 --> 00:06:13.512
of ownership. Fairfax financial holdings is a Canadian firm. Employees frame the privatization

00:06:13.512 --> 00:06:19.212
as a risk to employment stability and to the bank's public character. The protest reflects broader

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:23.652
concern among staff about ownership changes in state-linked financial institutions.

00:06:24.232 --> 00:06:28.992
Job security is the first fear they name, and public control of the lender is the second.

00:06:29.712 --> 00:06:32.772
The federal government has not yet commented on the strike's impact.

00:06:33.312 --> 00:06:37.972
Their walkout is set for two days, starting Monday, unless that sale is called off.

00:06:38.861 --> 00:06:43.561
Rwanda is pushing in the right direction on cleaner mobility, reaching an agreement to assemble

00:06:43.561 --> 00:06:44.841
electric buses locally.

00:06:44.841 --> 00:06:50.021
All Africa reports a deal with Chinese firm cherry and eco-fleet solutions for more

00:06:50.021 --> 00:06:54.961
than 200 buses, beginning with public transport vehicles that already carry large numbers

00:06:54.961 --> 00:06:55.901
of daily riders.

00:06:56.541 --> 00:07:00.841
Assembly inside Rwanda, rather than full imports, is the point of the partnership.

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:06.181
Public buses were prioritized because they reach far more people each day than private cars.

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:10.741
Starting with those buses extends lower emissions beyond private car owners.

00:07:10.741 --> 00:07:16.261
The project needs coordination among the government, the Chinese partner, and local operators

00:07:16.261 --> 00:07:17.541
if production is to grow.

00:07:18.061 --> 00:07:22.641
Cleaner mobility here is being tried first on the routes ordinary commuters already use.

00:07:23.181 --> 00:07:27.821
Government, cherry, and eco-fleet solutions have to keep that coordination going past the

00:07:27.821 --> 00:07:28.361
first batch.

00:07:29.021 --> 00:07:34.461
Still on the day's list, near-final results show IOTOVA winning Bulgaria's presidential run-off

00:07:34.461 --> 00:07:36.321
in a vote focused on Ukraine ties.

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:42.521
An inspector general is auditing whether the Environmental Protection Agency or EPA followed

00:07:42.521 --> 00:07:45.761
federal rules on artificial intelligence or AI tools.

00:07:46.381 --> 00:07:51.441
Turkish student-built moonrovers are slated for China's Chang'e 8 lunar mission, even though

00:07:51.441 --> 00:07:54.121
Turkey signed the United States-led Artemis Accords.

00:07:54.721 --> 00:08:00.441
Beijing is expanding production of Type 071 amphibious transport docks, moving construction

00:08:00.441 --> 00:08:04.401
to a second shipyard and potentially increasing capacity for troop movement.

00:08:04.401 --> 00:08:10.501
Ryanair has warned of a possible pay freeze and higher fares, citing a potential 2 billion

00:08:10.501 --> 00:08:14.841
euro rise in fuel costs in 2028, linked to Middle East tensions.

00:08:15.441 --> 00:08:21.441
Anthrax has killed hippos in Varunga National Park in the Democratic Republic of Congo, compounding

00:08:21.441 --> 00:08:27.281
threats from drought and conflict to local wildlife. California has seen illegal border crossings drop

00:08:27.281 --> 00:08:32.981
sharply, with arrests down more than 93% from the previous peak under the prior administration.

00:08:32.981 --> 00:08:38.795
To really understand how an emergency alert can still reach a phone when ordinary networks fail,

00:08:39.115 --> 00:08:43.875
you have to follow the path the message takes. A lot of daily coverage treats a breached

00:08:43.875 --> 00:08:49.115
alert as simple vandalism. These systems are built as one of the few reliable channels left

00:08:49.115 --> 00:08:54.735
when phone networks and broadcast towers are damaged or jammed. Governments pre-load the apps

00:08:54.735 --> 00:09:00.815
on devices sold in the country. They push messages through dedicated servers that bypass normal cellular

00:09:00.815 --> 00:09:05.495
congestion. That is why the same app can still function when voice calls fail.

00:09:06.095 --> 00:09:09.675
This model was developed after earlier conflicts showed that traditional

00:09:09.675 --> 00:09:14.855
sirens and television alerts often reach too few people too late. This design

00:09:14.855 --> 00:09:19.675
creates a single point of failure. Once an attacker gains server access, false

00:09:19.675 --> 00:09:24.515
messages travel at the same speed and with the same authority as real ones. Users

00:09:24.515 --> 00:09:29.315
have only minutes to decide whether to act. When later stories assign blame, the

00:09:29.315 --> 00:09:31.795
The technical detail that sorts a claim is origin.

00:09:32.495 --> 00:09:36.055
Official server logs or a clone site that mimic the app's appearance.

00:09:36.695 --> 00:09:41.135
A concrete check in the next round of reporting is whether authorities publish those server

00:09:41.135 --> 00:09:44.235
access logs, or only issue verbal denials.

00:09:44.815 --> 00:09:49.575
That check helps separate verified technical evidence from unconfirmed attributions while

00:09:49.575 --> 00:09:51.755
conflict reporting is still moving fast.

00:09:52.535 --> 00:09:57.555
How quickly official channels issue a correction is another way to gauge whether the underlying system

00:09:57.555 --> 00:10:00.195
still has any resilience left after a breach.

00:10:01.112 --> 00:10:05.852
Comparing several regional outlets on one incident shows which facts are shared and which

00:10:05.852 --> 00:10:07.932
remain attached to a claim without evidence.

00:10:08.752 --> 00:10:14.072
France 24 sets the two hacks on one canvas as matching interference with civilian tools.

00:10:14.692 --> 00:10:19.612
Al Jazeera waits the speed of the radiation all clear and the expired caresson ceasefire.

00:10:20.332 --> 00:10:25.712
IDBI bank employees keep their nationwide strike into a second day, still calling on the

00:10:25.712 --> 00:10:29.192
federal government to cancel the sale to Fairfax Financial Holdings.

